#==============================================================================
# env.properties.aws-ol6
#
# Environment configuration for building an Oracle Linux 6 AWS AMI.
# Loaded by build-ol-aws-ami.sh via the --env option.
#
# Companion files for other Oracle Linux versions:
#   env.properties.aws-ol10  (Oracle Linux 10.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol9   (Oracle Linux 9.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol8   (Oracle Linux 8.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol7   (Oracle Linux 7.x — experimental)
#
#==============================================================================
# !!! IMPORTANT DEPRECATION NOTICE !!!
#==============================================================================
# Oracle Linux 6 reached end of Premier Support on 2021-03-31, and Extended
# Life Support (ELS) ended in 2024. The upstream oracle-linux-image-tools
# project DOES NOT ship a distr/ol6-slim/ directory at all, and the AWS
# cloud target explicitly rejects releases below OL8.
#
# build-ol-aws-ami.sh works around these gaps by:
#   1. Generating distr/ol6-slim/ at runtime (env.properties, image-scripts.sh,
#      ol6-ks.cfg, provision.sh) from templates embedded in the wrapper.
#   2. Applying a sed patch to cloud/aws/image-scripts.sh to remove the
#      "OL8 and above" guard (same as OL7).
#   3. Applying a sed patch to cloud/aws/provision.sh to skip the
#      "yum install kernel-uek-modules" line on OL6 (this package does NOT
#      exist in the OL6 UEKR4 repository; ENA/NVMe drivers are bundled
#      directly inside the kernel-uek RPM).
#
# As a result:
#
#   * This template is intended ONLY for verification, learning, and legacy
#     migration scenarios. Do NOT use the resulting AMI for production
#     workloads. Oracle has not shipped security updates for OL6 since 2024.
#   * The upstream tooling may break OL6 support without warning in a future
#     refactor. The runtime patches and runtime-generated distr/ol6-slim/
#     files will need to be re-evaluated when that happens.
#   * Oracle Linux 6 only supports x86_64 (no aarch64) and BIOS boot
#     (no UEFI / NitroTPM / Secure Boot).
#   * UEK Release 4 is the ONLY kernel choice that provides ENA/NVMe
#     drivers on OL6. UEK2/UEK3 lack these drivers; UEK5+ is not available
#     for OL6. RHCK 2.6.32 also lacks the ENA driver.
#   * AWS VM Import/Export officially marks Oracle Linux 6 as EOL. This
#     wrapper bypasses that policy by using `import-snapshot` + `register-image`.
#
# If you need an actively supported Oracle Linux on AWS, prefer the OL8 / OL9
# / OL10 templates in this directory.
#==============================================================================

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Required] Parameters consumed by oracle-linux-image-tools
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Workspace directory for the build. Requires 20GB+ of free space.
#
# Default: /tmp/ol6-build-ws (universally accessible by the qemu user)
#
# Notes:
#   * /tmp is sometimes mounted as tmpfs (RAM-backed) on modern Linux.
#     If your host has less than ~32 GB RAM, /tmp may be too small.
#     The script will detect this and warn at runtime.
#   * /tmp is cleared on reboot. If your build may span a reboot, prefer
#     /var/tmp/ol6-build-ws or /var/lib/ol6-build-ws.
WORKSPACE="/tmp/ol6-build-ws"

# Distribution slug.
# Note: distr/ol6-slim/ does NOT exist in the upstream repo; it is created
# at runtime by build-ol-aws-ami.sh from embedded templates.
DISTR="ol6-slim"

# Target cloud
CLOUD="aws"

# Oracle Linux 6 U10 x86_64 DVD ISO.
# Like OL7, the OL6 ISO filename uses the "Server-" infix.
ISO_URL="https://yum.oracle.com/ISOS/OracleLinux/OL6/u10/x86_64/OracleLinux-R6-U10-Server-x86_64-dvd.iso"

# SHA256 checksum of the ISO.
#
# When unset, the script auto-resolves it in this order:
#   1. ${ISO_CHECKSUM_URL}                 (if you set it explicitly)
#   2. ${ISO_URL}.sha256sum                (legacy; NOT AVAILABLE for OL6 -> 404)
#   3. https://linux.oracle.com/security/gpg/checksum/OracleLinux-R6-U10-Server-x86_64.checksum
#      (Oracle-published GPG-signed checksum)
#
# For OL6, route #3 is the only working path. Route #2 returns 404 on OL6
# mirrors, unlike OL7 where it was historically the primary route. Recent
# verification (2026-05) confirms route #2 also returns 404 for OL7/8/9/10
# on yum.oracle.com — route #3 is now the reliable path across all versions.
#
# Verified-good SHA256 (as of 2026-05):
# ISO_CHECKSUM="625044388ee60a031965a42a32f4c1de0c029268975edcd542fd14160e0dadcb"

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Optional] Image customization
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OS variant short-id used by virt-install / osinfo-query.
# Modern osinfo-db (libosinfo 1.11+, osinfo-db-20250606+) uses the 'ol6.X'
# convention. The existing detect_os_variant() candidate chain falls
# through to rhel6.10 on typical builders (functionally equivalent since
# RHEL 6 and OL6 are binary-compatible).
# To use the native 'ol6.X' entry explicitly:
# OS_VARIANT="ol6.10"

# libguestfs backend
# LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND="direct"

# Build number
BUILD_NUMBER="0"

# Swap (No on cloud)
SETUP_SWAP="No"

# SELinux
SELINUX="enforcing"

# Root filesystem (ext4 or xfs).
# OL6 does NOT support lvm/btrfs at this layer.
#
# Default: xfs (aligned with OL7/8/9/10 templates in this directory).
#
# OL6 + xfs compatibility notes:
#   * UEK Release 4 (kernel 4.1.12) includes full XFS support; ENA / NVMe
#     drivers are also bundled inside the kernel-uek RPM.
#   * Anaconda 13.21 (OL6.10) supports installing onto XFS as the root FS;
#     XFS was promoted from tech preview to fully supported in OL6.4 and
#     has been stable since OL6.6.
#   * /boot remains on ext4 because GRUB Legacy 0.97 (OL6) reads ext4 most
#     reliably. build-ol-aws-ami.sh's distr::kickstart logic is scoped to
#     rewrite only the root partition fstype to keep /boot on ext4 even
#     when ROOT_FS=xfs.
#   * The OL6 build pipeline has not been fully validated end-to-end with
#     ROOT_FS=xfs by the author; the static checks pass but a Phase C
#     real-build verification has not yet been performed.
#
# To revert to the historical OL6 default, set ROOT_FS="ext4".
ROOT_FS="xfs"

# Root volume size of the AMI (GB)
DISK_SIZE_GB="10"

# Enable serial console at runtime (required for the EC2 Serial Console)
SERIAL_CONSOLE_RUNTIME="Yes"

# Build-time boot mode (bios mandatory for OL6+AWS).
#
# THREE independent constraints all require "bios" for OL6+AWS:
#   1. oracle-linux-image-tools enforces "bios" for the AWS cloud target.
#   2. Upstream build-image.sh enforces "bios" for OL7 (and the OL6 patch
#      extends this to OL6 because OL6 anaconda has no UEFI support either).
#   3. OL6 anaconda 13.x predates UEFI install entirely.
BOOT_MODE_BUILD="bios"

# Kernel selection.
#
# CRITICAL for OL6+AWS:
#   * KERNEL="rhck" is NOT valid for AWS Nitro - RHCK 2.6.32 lacks ENA driver.
#   * KERNEL="uek" with UEK_RELEASE=4 is the ONLY working combination.
#     UEK4 (4.1.12-124.48.6 latest) contains ena.ko, nvme.ko, nvme-core.ko
#     bundled directly in the main kernel-uek RPM (no kernel-uek-modules
#     package exists on OL6 UEKR4).
KERNEL="uek"

# UEK release for OL6 (only 4 is valid).
# UEK2/UEK3 do not have ENA. UEK5/6/7 are not available for OL6.
UEK_RELEASE="4"

# Keep linux-firmware. Note: kernel-uek on OL6 has a hard install dependency
# on linux-firmware, so setting "No" here will be undone the next time a
# kernel update reinstalls linux-firmware.
# LINUX_FIRMWARE="No"

# Root password (debug only)
# ROOT_PASSWORD="password:ChangeMe123!"

# Root SSH public key
# ROOT_SSH_KEY="file:${HOME}/.ssh/id_rsa.pub"

# Enable cloud-init (provisions ec2-user via SSH key from EC2 metadata).
# Verified package: cloud-init-18.4-2.0.9.el6.x86_64 (latest in ol6_addons).
# Verified package: cloud-utils-growpart-0.27-9.el6.x86_64 (also in ol6_addons).
CLOUD_INIT="Yes"
CLOUD_USER="ec2-user"

# RPM update policy applied during provisioning.
#
# Values:
#   "yes"      Run `yum update -y` after the base install. This pulls every
#              package (including the kernel-uek) from the OL6 yum repos to
#              its latest available version, addressing kernel and userspace
#              vulnerabilities discovered after the ISO was published.
#   "security" Apply only security-tagged updates via yum-plugin-security.
#              Note: OL6 ELS ended in 2024, so the security feed may no longer
#              receive new advisories. "yes" remains the default for OL6 to
#              capture every available errata-tagged update.
#   "no"       Skip the update step; the resulting AMI ships only the
#              packages that came in the ISO. NOT recommended.
#
# The setting flows through Phase 4 of build-ol-aws-ami.sh into the upstream
# distr/ol6-slim/provision.sh distr::common_cfg routine generated at runtime.
UPDATE_TO_LATEST="yes"

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Required] AWS import parameters
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Region in which the AMI will be created.
#
# When this value is empty (or unset), build-ol-aws-ami.sh resolves it
# dynamically at runtime via EC2 Instance Metadata Service:
#   1. IMDSv2 (token-based; preferred)
#   2. IMDSv1 (legacy; used only if IMDSv2 fails)
#   3. Fallback constant "ap-northeast-1" (used outside EC2)
#
# Set an explicit region here to override the auto-detection.
AWS_REGION=""

# S3 bucket used as the staging area for the VMDK upload.
# Created automatically (with public access blocked) if it does not exist.
#
# Shared across all OL versions in this directory (env.properties.aws-ol{6,7,
# 8,9,10}). The S3_KEY_PREFIX below provides per-version isolation, so the
# single vmimport IAM role policy created by setup-vmimport-role.sh covers
# every version's import.
S3_BUCKET="my-oracle-linux-ami-import-bucket"
S3_KEY_PREFIX="ol6-ami-import"

# AMI_NAME="OracleLinux-6-U10-x86_64-$(date +%Y%m%d)"
# AMI_DESCRIPTION="Oracle Linux 6 Update 10 (x86_64) custom AMI"

# AMI boot mode.
# OL6 produces legacy-bios only (no UEFI / NitroTPM / Secure Boot).
BOOT_MODE="legacy-bios"

VMIMPORT_ROLE_NAME="vmimport"
